  "articleBody": "Adding or replacing an exterior basement door is rarely as simple as hanging a standard bedroom door. Basement entries face constant hydrostatic pressure, soil contact, and intense rain runoff. If the frame is set incorrectly, you risk water pouring across your lower level during the next heavy storm.\n\nWhat Can Change the Right Choice\nBefore signing a contract, examine how the contractor plans to manage exterior grading and drainage. EPA guidelines emphasize that unresolved moisture issues outside must be fixed before remodeling below grade. If downspouts dump water near the threshold, a new door cannot stop structural dampness.\n\n- Opening integrity: Concrete and masonry cutting requires verify whether the wall is load-bearing.\n- Water protection: Ensure the scope includes a continuous sill pan, head flashing, and proper weatherstripping.\n- Code specifics: Exterior basement exits often need compliant landings, exterior stairs, guards, or emergency egress clearances depending on your local building department.\n\nWhen your opening needs structural enlargement, concrete cutting, or exterior drainage corrections, hiring an experienced finish and remodeling crew is critical. Abraham Becerra and the crew at HH Remodeling LLC handle framing, finish carpentry, and general exterior repairs across Denver and Aurora. Call 303-505-0866 to talk through your basement entrance.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}